  "text": "Recipe: Jalapeño & Kale Corn Bread\nCreator: Sharmila Vedam\nCategory: Baked Good\nIngredients: cornmeal, buckwheat flour, sprouted wheat flour, kale, jalapeños, soy milk, apple cider vinegar (ACV), maple syrup, nutritional yeast, baking powder, baking soda, salt\nCooking methods: bake, no-cook\nInstructions: + Mix all the dry ingredients and set aside\n+ Mix soy milk with ACV. Let it curdle.\n+ BATTER: Combine curdled soy milk with all the dry ingredients. Add finely chopped kale, Jalapeños & maple syrup to the mixture. Add some water if needed.\n+ Pour the batter to a silicone muffin tray. Garnish each muffin with a thinly sliced Jalapeño on top.\n+ Bake at 350F for about 15-18 mins.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (cornmeal, buckwheat flour or sprouted wheat flour), BEANS (soy milk), LEAFY GREENS (kale), HERBS & SPICES.",
